-- Act I: Desk Interaction
--
PRIMARY_NARRATOR: The wooden chair creaks under your weight. The desk surface is littered with half-filled sheets, ink smudges, and the black cast-iron bulk of the typewriter.
FADING_LOGIC: The case file is still open to page seventeen. Three sentences drafted since dawn. The grammar is fractured, the deductions unmoored.
OBSESSIVE_DREAD: It's slipping away. If you don't anchor the sequence before morning, the whole case collapses into white noise. But your eyes won't focus. The keys are blurring into black teeth.
PRIMARY_NARRATOR: You cannot write another word. Your skull feels hollowed out, scraping behind your temples. #end
